# Transient run logs from a development session. These were swept in once by an
# accidental `git add -A`; they are console output, not results, and one of them
# carried a superseded present-value cost that contradicted the paper.
*.log
*.err
!code/results/*.log

# LaTeX list-of-figures / list-of-tables are regenerated by every build and only
# add diff noise.
paper/*.lof
paper/*.lot
paper/ae_submission/*.lof
paper/ae_submission/*.lot
paper/ae_submission/*.log
paper/ae_submission/*.toc

# Internal working material. These are the authoring and QA record, not part of the
# research artefact the Data Availability Statement promises ("model code, input-data
# provenance, country profiles and figure generators"). They stay on disk and in git
# history; they are simply not part of the public tree a referee lands in.
paper/NOTE_TO_ABDUL.md
paper/pipeline/
paper/_qc3/
paper/_w2_review.txt
paper/AE_STYLE_ANATOMY.md
paper/AE_WORDING_PLAYBOOK.md
paper/APPLIED_ENERGY_PLAN.md
paper/RESTRUCTURE_v5_PLAN.md
paper/PRODUCTION_PIPELINE.md
paper/STYLE_GUIDE.md
paper/HPFIX_FACTS.md
paper/meeting_briefing.*
paper/meeting_*_summary.md
paper/dispatch_briefing.*
REVIEW_A3_sensitivity.json

# Superseded submission deliverables. V5.pdf and SI.pdf are the current pair; the
# versioned copies are recoverable from git history.
paper/ae_submission/Paper_AE_v*.pdf
paper/ae_submission/Paper_AE_v*.docx
paper/ae_submission/SI_v*.pdf

# Agent audit reports. Internal working material, kept out of the public tree on the
# same principle as paper/_qc3/ and REVIEW_A3_sensitivity.json: what belongs in the
# repository is the corrected manuscript and the checks that keep it correct, not the
# reports that prompted the corrections. The reports live on disk during a review round
# and their findings land in the prose, the gate, or a commit message.
reviews/

# Style corpus: published Applied Energy articles supplied by the co-author as
# writing-style reference. These are copyrighted Elsevier PDFs and their text
# extractions, held locally as an input to the style pass. This repository is cited
# as a public archive, so redistributing them here would breach the publisher's
# terms. Nothing in the manuscripts depends on them.
paper/style_corpus/
